Index: openwiki/.claims/quickstart.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/quickstart.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/quickstart.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,88 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:cc1e232787cca6b4a43123445d68b4451f0d9d683d7b0c2c82a673e0744cb3da",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7a98d03ab3f74901966ddc6ecc0d870b",
+      "statement": "A node is one celld process, the nodes that share one bucket are a fleet, and a cell is a Durable Object with its own SQLite database; a conditional bucket write grants a node ownership of a cell, so there is no membership protocol or consensus service.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L14-L22",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b38ea33b7d2476112bec9c830f0bcea697b8beb3d3543387d9c9f48aae44b89e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_554775407c50467c9067ffaf847ec943",
+      "statement": "celld dev starts one node and a local object store with no Docker or cloud bucket, serving the Worker listener at http://127.0.0.1:9876 by default, keeping durable state in .celld/dev, and rebuilding after source or configuration changes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L92-L116",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8074129e03a60260cb7590223e72d3c1e034fa3f5c4ac8f0bb06d5e8075cb228:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L274-L337",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b096c5a5ad9975c4ab325103a929173350dcf5ea6b34e00c21e7a87adbc07d7d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8c5e220d694e4c95b83e18f6a71491ba",
+      "statement": "celld deploy accepts an s3://, gs://, or az:// bucket with the appropriate credentials, and a gs:// or az:// bucket takes no S3 endpoint.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L118-L141",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4308a90aa82ef83f745225bbeff40202f42ac38e98b5979af54f0e32b269197:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L126-L208",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2a43c86b5bf272db648816ef280679e486228563aa65aa8362c2bdcacd0b4050:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8850e7d3324e4e47be1c843156a038a9",
+      "statement": "One node proves each write through the bucket so a write costs one storage round trip; with two or more nodes celld sends each write to a follower and acknowledges once it holds the data on disk.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L134-L147",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80a3a29ab9fe62f30a99cf7ff0e3ebee709992b05d240dd7d6e5fb42c04fa762:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d9608591a31b4702813dddab5c509e85",
+      "statement": "SIGTERM or SIGINT makes a node drain gracefully, reporting unhealthy, finishing accepted requests, and handing cells to compatible peers, and the orchestrator stop grace must be longer than CELLD_SHUTDOWN_TOTAL_MS (default 40000).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L427-L512",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc113c75ece7790c0969fc617b8a10b233c0ac7f572cb41fd0a6a040b9d64095:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a3395711d2164339bf2f9874ef2b3cd7",
+      "statement": "The bucket must provide conditional writes and read-after-write consistency, and celld diagnose tests the store because one that silently ignores the condition cannot fence a cell.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L16-L74",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9bb03e07b2401f85efa583b3f31beb2893e20fb147c729ba91aaf6577565d0dc:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cc48b7e4673f48f8a864da0392900c09",
+      "statement": "Peer traffic is plaintext HTTP and the fleet HMAC does not encrypt it, so the advertised addresses must be placed on a trusted private network or an encrypted overlay.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md",
+          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:d7726a326cd998305fef572fcf14f0e067eda591affa871526ed566ab91f21c2"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T14:20:08.241Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/storage/cell-storage.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/storage/cell-storage.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/storage/cell-storage.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:069477cd811731ab6968f6c1a185078be766f9b23d3362b3ea8567a41e6d1ceb",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a85c9e6c1bcb43f4832d4728419d1620",
+      "statement": "The Durable Object storage API is backed by per-cell SQLite: async in JS but synchronous underneath, with sync Rust ops wrapped in async by the JS harness, and each cell owning its own database file and epoch-fenced bucket prefix.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L6-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70efb51767a5944f51fe86cb6ba9c9e77e1d0b44753431b624eafda074c770a4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_96bf9d3535874c718e6b0c69f4feda29",
+      "statement": "Cell storage state belongs to the isolate, not a thread, because a cell event's turns run on whatever tokio worker holds the isolate; no synchronization is needed because a turn holds the isolate lock.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L22-L33",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2e51a6e757a89997357e57c46af40a38d425b7923d2f828bd839d117261c9d12:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c4dde8a4ecd546b7aa436893e3124e20",
+      "statement": "Each open cell couples its SQLite connection with the ownership epoch that authorized its activation, one residency invariant that prevents asynchronous work from recovering an epoch through a later ownership lookup after a takeover.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L52-L60",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0aee592c5655ca94f7a60d89cfe0c73b0d7f14485d7750992756f8a7017742ee:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7ff211f9186a4d5ab6238b58153678dd",
+      "statement": "The storage ops surface converts V8 values to Rust, calls into storage, and converts the answer back; the storage semantics live in storage.rs and the value serialization format lives in storage_ops.rs because it is what JS can see.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/js/storage_ops.rs#L3-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5ca4a3526d6627c2ba4cc1b3581dc46c41b918be8e3fd5132db5d566bdc53731:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_60c38f37f58141afa71d26e884df3211",
+      "statement": "A schema cookie caches PRAGMA schema_version because the pragma takes a shared pager lock, and a handler that touches no storage would otherwise pay two locked reads per event.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/storage.rs#L62-L80",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:beecdf1f9bd78a70d0af124b8fcabf6abbdc81f856489c65eca791910f8a1229:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bce189de689749ad9c794fd8509e2280",
+      "statement": "A failed SQLite operation poisons the actor only when a critical engine error (SQLITE_FULL, SQLITE_IOERR, SQLITE_NOMEM, SQLITE_INTERRUPT) coincides with a destroyed transaction (autocommit re-enabled); anything else recovers.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/sqlite.rs#L15-L28",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef604ef62b0f43c0766fca3fd0f412c48cc1300ffbfd3c3dcddaeb5501ae2e76:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_1cb38cf68a7a4ad28c9c3693e72db716",
+      "statement": "A KV namespace is a cell (__KvNamespace) whose bounds ship as data the JS harness compares against; keys are at most 512 bytes, values 25 MiB, metadata 1 KiB, expiry below 60 s is refused, and a list page returns at most 1000 keys.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/kv.rs#L3-L17",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f611a4a3f012d7bf8c9542d6e2ad91bbd7ee1984e97bae117211e0aa21bb3e6a:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/kv.rs#L37-L65",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a23b19f7a21c2fb174fcd5be3240fed88ef43f66e1bcca3cace806ff1b14cdc:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_71a9e352f801401eb44389b74704fefd",
+      "statement": "The largest value stored inline in a KV namespace cell is 1 MiB (MAX_INLINE_VALUE_BYTES), chosen by a measured latency crossover; larger values go to the fleet bucket and the row names them.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/kv.rs#L41-L56",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b1f8b22bbc8989ffc6176bc2698eaf2f8f43022154bbe3cf1b6c855fd30a4252:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f533d1832aeb43b3baf5aa9ceef7d8e7",
+      "statement": "Large KV values are epoch-qualified references (v2:e<epoch>:<digest>) stored under kv/blobs-v2/<cell>/e<epoch>/<digest>; a new write must use exactly the activation's epoch, and only objects from the collector's epoch or older are collectable.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/kv.rs#L169-L208",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b924d872cacd1a2b216a373177d5b1e98fdfeef1167f5a77ce6fdad667496c0c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5ff2416c377e469b8db1f71aaf1efbe7",
+      "statement": "A D1 binding result can contain at most 100,000 rows or 32 MiB, and celld refuses invalid UTF-8 from a SQLite TEXT value.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/cloudflare-compat.md#L110-L116",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a22c49ba6cfbc3f053f9d7a6c74dfedbb3551d35ece17f0484e800ceecb33845:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f90c29faedde4d10860ff33ac26a1cb8",
+      "statement": "Each cell database is opened in WAL mode with wal_autocheckpoint(0) and a long-running read lock, and the ltx Db captures each committed write as L0 LTX segments at <watch>/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/db.sqlite.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/db.rs#L5-L32",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60803d35c6fffb5df8771fb8fac45fdd5cf78d102ae6954638c1e9156954a778:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T14:20:08.241Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/testing/verification.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/testing/verification.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/testing/verification.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:869704d304a98e92d01dce93ce2c7025bf8d230a9d2a20fe1cc6da975abd9975",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5589d9f8b95b44f9a26a8f6fc689f6ad",
+      "statement": "celld tests three promises at the layer where a failure shows most clearly: the API contract by differential execution against the Cloudflare runtime, the coordination protocol by an exhaustively model-checked TLA+ specification and by deterministic simulation, and the full system by fault injection on live fleets.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L3-L15",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c35dfb12c74927175e44471c13a51bc7a04cea4711aceddc62702469c215749e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_38156e8d5a2943f0814c3b3b313262d0",
+      "statement": "The conformance harness runs each Workers and Durable Objects program twice, once on workerd and once on celld on identical bytes, and requires the outputs to be equal.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L17-L25",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24dcc1be53d2a74cc9eb19414dc4c5da519e867623552857d200e0a8753f747c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2de9d477ffdf4004989f74eb1ea3d44d",
+      "statement": "The coordination protocol is specified in TLA+; the checker enumerates every reachable state at a small configuration, each configuration carries a pinned expected verdict (mostly failures modeling bugs the protocol once had), and the specifications are a hand-synced snapshot deliberately not in CI.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L37-L79",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4f0c41467af8be33f19852ba70078e4739940bef8e8cc2be0b3a61cc2cf383c5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_28ed366eab8d4aa48c9857af801c4566",
+      "statement": "The coordination protocol is a pure decision core with no I/O of its own; a seeded deterministic simulator injects latency, compare-and-swap races, lost responses, clock drift, and crashes at each await point, and checks safety and liveness properties across millions of schedules, with the checkers themselves tested against deliberately broken variants.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L81-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56c5dc08f00838c93cdd8047179e4a80f2072fe5bc4d9c44f2b8d69ea2cdbe73:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_154e7d0f0b27425aa46fe317fd369b3e",
+      "statement": "A permanent fleet lab qualifies each release with real buckets and fault injection between verification passes, attacking SIGKILL mid-write, frozen owners, nodes cut off from the bucket, 429-throttled stores, and provider-level host stops; no acknowledged write was lost across every run.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L110-L155",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3706f7d7a74c80fc864f2d04e8f4a63424f1083fd407e9e99ef8561c92566356:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3603ad0a696048d6b5fe608ff390b51d",
+      "statement": "Measured results include 5,500 ownership attempts with zero violations, a warm resident request at p50 ~1.1 ms and p99 ~7 ms with zero bucket operations, and ten 8 GB nodes holding 10,000 resident cells and 20,000 concurrent WebSockets with data restored in ~11 s at the tail after two nodes stopped.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L162-L186",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e58b337292b91a9dc3a8b4f5719fa8880d6dbe4edcb5d0a77a5231ecdb995d32:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f8978085e8464b6da21d1b598967a2ed",
+      "statement": "celld-logic is a pure decision core with no async, I/O, clocks, randomness, or locks and no unit-test target of its own (test=false); the celld library include!s the conformance and internal suites behind the celld_internal_tests cfg and can swap the real asyncrt for the deterministic simulator.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L300-L318",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca5ec31a21e264fd2c4c2d6361d832f928702246e81be384090e03af5da78321:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/Cargo.toml#L5-L7",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fffbc34deac4707ab090c564a5bbd985fe904e60de98e7eb4336d59985035892:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6d60f6f3339a4bb9a0df8334635a1781",
+      "statement": "The lab measures the reserve-headroom edge on both sides: a fleet full to its resident limit has no space for the cells of a lost node, so a failure of more than one node at the limit degrades the service.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L189-L196",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:07e167f2cf3d1c2b088dff84174c38ab438bc6e569769b3a2da488c1d05af673:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T14:20:08.241Z"
+  }
+}

